    {
        "content": "<p>Is this a bad idea or are we just missing this simp lemma:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">grind</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">lemma</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">test</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">@</span><span class=\"n\">Membership</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Finset</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">SetLike</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">instMembership</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">↔</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">@</span><span class=\"n\">Membership</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Finset</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Finset</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">instMembership</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>I have a few instances of this problem in my project where this would help</p>",
        "id": 583429857,
